@startuml fig4_action_chain
' Diagram 4 of the IEC 60050-351 pattern: the action chain of test case 2,
' after Figure 2 of the standard.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' What it shows: the nine action lines of test case 2 as the chain of
' functional units they run between, with the letter of the figure legend each
' line carries. Line M8 ends at the comparing element that M3 starts from, so
' the chain is a cycle. Test case 3 has the same property with an open action,
' which is the point the caption has to make.
'
' Drawn as a flow rather than as a class diagram, since what matters here is
' the shape of the chain, not the class hierarchy. Each box is one functional
' unit of the test model, each edge one action line.
'
' Left out on purpose: the physical units realising these functional units, the
' groupings the standard draws as dashed frames, and the variables as
' individuals. All three are in the test model and in diagram 2.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam nodesep 26
skinparam ranksep 34
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 13
  BorderThickness 1
}

rectangle "CommandSourceB" as SRC
rectangle "ReferenceGeneratorB" as REF
rectangle "ComparingElementB" as CMP
rectangle "ControllingElementB" as CTL
rectangle "ActuatorB" as ACT
rectangle "ValveB" as VAL
rectangle "ControlledSystemB" as SYS
rectangle "MeasuringElementB" as MSR
rectangle "FinalVariableGenerationB" as FIN

' Top to bottom, so the returning line M8 is the only edge running upwards and
' the cycle is visible as such.
SRC --> REF : "M1  c"
REF --> CMP : "M2  w"
CMP --> CTL : "M3  e"
CTL --> ACT : "M4  m"
ACT --> VAL : "M5  y"
VAL --> SYS : "M6  y"
SYS --> MSR : "M7  x"
MSR --> CMP : "M8  r"
SYS --> FIN : "M9  q"

@enduml
